  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 24th June 2003, the proposed basement extension having a total volume of 50m3, would be lawful within the meaning of section 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe proposed development falls within Class A of Part 1 of Schedule 2 of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995. Planning permission is therefore not required.\r\n\r\n\r\nInformative:\r\nTo be considered lawful under Class A of Part 1 Schedule 2 of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995, the works should not include the provision of an associated a sunken garden, retaining wall or fencing in the front garden.\r\n"
